    "summary": "Malicious code in aurum-pay (PyPI)",
    "details": "When using the library, it silently executes remote commands and installs the next-stage payload. On linux, the payload is a binary. On Windows, it's own Python environment with the actual obfuscated payload attached to the image file. Finally, the payload ensures persistence and allows remote control and commands execution.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-11-aurum-pay\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - Downloads and executes a remote executable.\n\n\n - obfuscation\n\n\n - action-hidden-in-lib-usage\n\n\n - Downloads and executes a remote malicious script.\n\n\n - rat\n\n\n - persistence\n\n",
